you know boba fett as an original star  wars trilogy villain but did you know he  could actually get worse from planting  bombs to almost killing a baby these are  the worst things boba fett has ever done  in his first canonical appearance after  attack of the clones boba fett pursued a  quest of vengeance against mace windu  the jedi responsible for beheading his  father jango fett this plot unfolded in  the second season of star wars the clone  wars during the episode death trap in  the episode a young fett takes on the  identity of a clone trooper named lucky  with this disguise he's able to  infiltrate mace windu's quarters and  place a motion-activated bomb in his  room all in the hopes of murdering the  jedi and finally getting revenge for his  dad while fett is successful in both  planting and setting off the bomb it  doesn't end up killing his intended  target an innocent clone trooper is  instead slaughtered after inadvertently  setting the bomb off but in the wake of  this unintentional killing fett doesn't  give up on his plans for vengeance  though he's initially reluctant he  decides to attack the reactor core of a  republic star destroyer if it works it's  a plan that wouldn't just kill windu but  also everyone else on board through his  bombing plan and subsequent unsuccessful  attack on the reactor core it's clear  that fett is seriously grappling with  the loss of his father by inflicting  more pain on others and it's also  apparent that he's more than willing to  kill anyone who gets in the way of his  target he may still be a kid but fett's  already brutal beyond his years a few  seasons after his first appearance in  the clone wars fett returned a little  older but still just as dangerous in  season four's bounty bet had become an  even more hardened soul thanks to an  extended prison sentence no longer just  seeking revenge for his father that was  inching closer to his portrayal in the  empire strikes back by making a living  as a bounty hunter to pursue this goal  fett partnered with a squad of fellow  hunters got a mask to conceal his  identity and took a job delivering a  large chest to the powerful ruler otua  blanc while on his delivery mission it  was revealed that the chest didn't  contain jewels or weapons but instead  held a young woman named pluma sodi who  was being sent to blank as a forced  bride when darkseid force user asajj  ventress who'd briefly joined fett's  crew for this assignment realized what  their true cargo was she hesitated but  while the former sith apprentice had a  crisis of conscience fett demonstrated  his growing darkness by remaining firmly  committed to the task at hand in fat's  previous clone wars story he seemed  uncertain about hurting innocent people  but this time pluma sodi's suffering  fell on deaf ears that's ruthlessness  sometimes manifests in shooting  adversaries and other times it emerges  in ignoring the cries of the helpless  while it may seem like the empire  strikes back was the first instance of  boba fett and darth vader crossing paths  media outside of the movies has made it  apparent that the two characters met  before one such encounter came in  marvel's 2015 star wars comic series  which saw boba fett being hired by darth  vader to track down a figure who'd  worked alongside obi-wan kenobi during  the events of a new hope now on the hunt  for his bounty fett was willing to  achieve his goal by any means necessary  including murder while trying to track  down his target fett encountered a  number of people including rodians and a  group of moisture farmers that he  interrogated for information once they  told him what he needed to know they  weren't released back to their humdrum  lives but instead were promptly killed  by phet this approach even extended to  an unnamed farmer at the moss icely  cantina who after being viciously  interrogated dropped a bombshell  revelation to fete that the man he was  looking for was named luke skywalker in  one 